{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1521739-why-dracula-choosed-to-be-embraced-by-lambach","id":1521739,"title":"Why Dracula choosed to be embraced by Lambach?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-08-31T03:40:27-07:00","id":1521739,"title":"Why Dracula choosed to be embraced by Lambach?","content":"Hey!<br /> I'm the ST of the Transilvanian Chronicles and my game is at the end of book 2.<br /> In act 3 Dracula has prisoners:<br /> Lambach 5th gen and Tabac 4th gen. Dracula seems to have a decent idea on how generations and diablery work.<br /> <br /> Why did he choose to get embraced by Lambach (becoming a 6th) and then diablerize Tabac (becoming a 5th), rather than getting embraced by Tabac and then diablerizing him being a 4th as a result??<br /> <br /> I'm one game session away from this to happen and I need to come up with an explanation that is not &quot;harmful for the common sense&quot; of my players. So far, I've only come up with the idea of having Tabac in torpore and without blood, but if that's the case I believe it's quite probably one of my players pushes Dracula aside and tries diablerizeing Tabac themself. My player's characters are already 400 years old Tzimisce and they were active militants to destroy the elders of the clan and form the New Clan Tzimisce.\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11010-ersito","name":"erSito","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11010_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-31T06:11:34-07:00","id":1521746,"title":"","content":"My theory is that Dracula tortured and threatened both vampires, Lambach is sometimes portrayed as a coward, Tabak was probably a different animal, Dracula may have noticed that Tabak would kill him and not complete the Embrace, unlike Lambach.<br /> I can imagine Tabak captured taunting and threatening Lambach right after Dracula's Embrace.<br /> Lambach knew he would not get away with Embracing Dracula.<br /> Dracula, aware that Tabak would take revenge on both of them, decided to commit diablerie on Tabak to put an end to the vengeful elder.\u200b<br /> <br /> Another possibility would be for Dracula to convince Lambach to commit diablerie on Tabak together, and thus Dracula becomes 5th generation, and Lambach 4th generation, but the mechanical weirdness part is up to the Storyteller.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12210,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12210-ulisses","user":"Ulisses","date":". 08-31-2023, 09:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12210-ulisses","name":"Ulisses","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-31T08:42:46-07:00","id":1521752,"title":"","content":"The relationship between Lambach, Dracula, and Tabak, is one of those topics in Vampire: the Masquerade, that has a lot of conspiratorial thinking around it, at least in part due to the exact weirdness that you're pointing out. It kind of *doesn't* make sense, and that's a plot hook you can do something with.<br /> <br /> There are various theories out there to try and explain what's actually going on during Dracula's Embrace. One of the more common features is the idea that Lambach is more powerful and more cunning than most people think, and this whole thing was part of a ploy.<br /> <br /> One possible theory:<br /> <br /> Lambach posed as Tabak's childe as a way of keeping heat off of himself. Tabak may have even been mentally manipulated with Dominate to believe all of it.<br /> <br /> Dracula ends up being similarly manipulated, without realizing. Getting him to diablerize Tabak is a way to keep Dracula from potentially digging into the matter if he eventually discovers that his Generation is lower than it would be if Lambach was as weak as he was supposed to be, and to give Dracula a false sense of confidence regarding his relationship with his sire.<br /> <br /> (A little more detail. In this theory, Lambach is a Fourth Generation, childe of The Eldest It/Themself. Tabak would be Fifth Generation if Lambach was his sire, or Sixth Generation if he was Lambach's grand-childe. Dracula, Embraced by Lambach, would be Fifth Generation. Diablerizing Tabak would have no practical value for Dracula's Generation, but would be an explanation for why Dracula ends up with the same Generation his sire is SUPPOSED to have.)<br /> <br /> Also note that the Embrace and diablerie conveniently occur with third-party witnesses at least nearby, people who can say that they saw Lambach get played, putting the blame for all of this squarely on Dracula's shoulders.<br /> <br /> And if Lambach was a Fourth Generation, you could potentially imagine him using an Elder-level Dominate power (or a Dominate/Presence amalgam might make more sense) that helps the story spread; only a handful of the most powerful Cainites would be able to potentially resist, which would make rewriting a historical record not too difficult if the few capable of overcoming the Discipline didn't care to correct matters publicly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-31T08:46:08-07:00","id":1521753,"title":"","content":"Vlad was well versed of the workings and rumors of the Clan<br /> He was the member of the Basarab Ravenant family that split when a Basarab became the King of Wallachia into the Danesti and Draculesti branches; the Draculesti branch birthed him and he came under the guidance of Count Rustovich and Count Radu, two of the most influential figures among the Cainites of Transylvania and he almost became the Child of none other than Yorak him/her/itself! <br /> Not to mention, it is rumored the Shadow Lords have some cards on the table too regarding Vlad and of course, thanks in part to the tutelage of the Ravnos oracle Durga Syn, Vlad know many things he not spuosed to<br /> When he narrowly escaped from the Cathedral alive, his desire to gain the Embrace on <i>his own terms</i> redoubled.<br /> <br /> Lambach was a weak willed fool, was famous about that and of his incompetence (of course it is possible Lambach played a long con)<br /> As per the Children of Inquisition, \u200bLambach was a noble-born Tzimisce, member of the now gone Ruthvenski Family, raised in Eastern Europe specifically to become undead, bred to wield power. Unfortunately, the side effect of controlled breeding creates spoiled childer with weak genes and weaker wills. Thus, Lambach never wielded his command with much confidence or courage. He was a rather indecisive vampire lord. He lived his life in fear of the inevitable Embrace and tried his best to avoid it. Because he spent so much time dreading the bite, he suffered greatly when his sire, Tabak, drained him of his blood. As a vampire, he became an anxiety-ridden, desperate, terrified bully<br /> <br /> At the end of the day, wen Tabak and Lambach ended up staked and the prisoners of Vlad, he had a <i>choice</i><br /> And the Embrace is something you do it by accidenet sometimes, but needs your, lets say participation - drain your future child and give her your blood when she is &quot;empty and basically dead&quot;<br /> Tabak would never done this, he was a powerfull Matuselah - as soon as Vlad would have removed the stake would have ended up lunch to a very hungry and angry Ancient<br /> While Lambach? <br /> It was easy to &quot;convince&quot; him to do the deed and watch his sire die<br /> Of course this playd in Lambach's favor, so he might not be that idiot waek willed fool many belived... after all, he survived the Anarch Revolt and offed his Sire with Vlad","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-31T10:09:24-07:00","id":1521756,"title":"","content":"I would go with the idea is that Dracula could manipulate Lambach Ruthaven as he is depicted as he is cunning survivor and will do what is good for him and saw a chance to get rid somebody that he disliked. Not to mention is that Vlad Dracula had a strong notion on how the clan worked and knew more from Durga Syn council of what could work for him and I'm sure she told him a good bit on what kind of kindred that his future sire is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 08-31-2023, 01:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-31T13:12:55-07:00","id":1521771,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1521739-why-dracula-choosed-to-be-embraced-by-lambach?p=1521753#post1521753\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He was the member of the Basarab Ravenant family that split when a Basarab became the King of Wallachia into the Danesti and Draculesti branches; the Draculesti branch birthed him and he came under the guidance of Count Rustovich and Count Radu, two of the most influential figures among the Cainites of Transylvania and he almost became the Child of none other than Yorak him/her/itself!</div> </div> </div> </div>This is another example of how canon has been changed by subsequent authors retconning things. There's nothing wrong with going with the latest version of canon if you like it, but the information in Transylvanian Chronicles clearly contradicts what was originally established in Children of the Inquisition. This is why on so many levels I now view Revised era canon to simply be its own &quot;Earth-2&quot; world that has the same character names and concepts as the 1e/2e &quot;Earth-1&quot; WoD, but is in fact a different setting entirely.<br /> <br /> It doesn't make sense to me why so famous a line as the House of Basarab could possibly be Revenants. Wouldn't people notice the family living for centuries longer and not seeming to age? Some forgotten, minor, ancient boyar family rotting away at its small family manor is one thing. Being the Princes of Wallachia and interacting with the other famous nobles of Europe (and intermarrying with them) is another.<br /> <br /> Originally, Dracula's knowledge of the Tzimisce came from his father's membership in the Order of the Dragon and its knights' vampire hunting lore as well as information provided by Durga Syn (who often had the role of being a &quot;good&quot; vampire that helps other against her own kind). It wasn't because their family had been Revenants for the past several thousand years.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>erSito</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1521739-why-dracula-choosed-to-be-embraced-by-lambach#post1521739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm one game session away from this to happen and I need to come up with an explanation that is not &quot;harmful for the common sense&quot; of my players. So far, I've only come up with the idea of having Tabac in torpore and without blood, but if that's the case I believe it's quite probably one of my players pushes Dracula aside and tries diablerizeing Tabac themself. My player's characters are already 400 years old Tzimisce and they were active militants to destroy the elders of the clan and form the New Clan Tzimisce.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> <br /> If I remember correctly, there was no Tabak in the original biography of Dracula in Children of the Inquisition. He's an addition made in the Transylvania Chronicles, likely because the authors (or perhaps an editorial mandate from the Developer) wanted a new scene for the PCs to witness. Because they thought their idea was cool, they didn't care that it violated canon. Or because they wanted to deliberately change it because they didn't like some of the earlier canon.<br /> <br /> You may just want to ignore that new information in Transylvania Chronicles II. Just have Dracula force Lambach to embrace him and gets his generation that way. He never diablerizes Tabak. Tabak can just be some companion/pack member of Lambach's that can get ambushed by the PCs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-31T13:37:49-07:00","id":1521773,"title":"","content":"Maybe Lambach Ruthhaven is more dangerous then most are willing to give credit for and it seems that Tzismce itself seems quite fond of him and takes steps to protect his childe or grand childe from any dangers. I really should look this fiend up in more detail.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-01T11:30:36-07:00","id":1521827,"title":"","content":"Now that I've read more on Lambach Ruthaven from a wide variety of vtm sites. I'm starting to think that maybe he is more powerful and dangerous then most are willing to give credit and poses as somebody less dangerous so that he gets overlooked and perhaps is playing a truly long game and that the Eldest really admires the strategy and takes steps to protect Lambach out of some lingering sense of affection.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-01T12:45:14-07:00","id":1521830,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1521739-why-dracula-choosed-to-be-embraced-by-lambach?p=1521771#post1521771\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I remember correctly, there was no Tabak in the original biography of Dracula in Children of the Inquisition.</div> </div> </div> </div>I just noticed that I was wrong about this after rereading some of Children of the Inquisition again. While I don't think Tabak was referenced in the Dracula section, Dracula capturing Lambach and Tabak, forcing Lambach to embrace him, and then diablerizing Tabak is mentioned in the Lambach Ruthven section of Children of the Inquisition.<br /> <br /> So no retcon. This is original lore. My bad.<br /> <br /> However, according to that same section, the Camarilla Justicars defeated both Lambach and Tabak. Tabak was put into torpor. Lambach was captured, but before the Justicars could destroy both of them, Dracula (as a mortal) intervened. He destroyed the weakened Justicars. The reason Dracula made Lambach embrace him is easy - Lambach was very weak, but still awake. Tabak was already in torpor, so he was not capable of embracing anyone. Dracula already knew enough vampire lore to realize Tabak was Lambach's sire and thus had more potent blood. So after Lambach embraced him, he diablerized the helpless Tabak.<br /> <br /> I don't know if TC2 explained that explicitly, or if they made some minor modifications. But I think the above clearly describes why Dracula did what he did. It also is very similar to the poster's original idea &quot;of having Tabac in torpore and without blood&quot;. Which means he is quite right about the potential of his 400 year old PCs simply diablerizing Tabak first.<br /> <br /> That probably shows a great flaw of the TC adventures which are designed to heavily railroad PCs into witnessing canonical NPC events, but not intended to allow PCs to alter them in any way. The only way I can think that the PCs being prevented from changing things is that they themselves are defeated earlier (by the Camarilla Justicars that defeated Tabak and Lambach?) and weakened (perhaps even torpored themselves but later revived by Dracula or Lambach) so they cannot diablerize Tabak themselves. This is probably another railroad as STs cannot guarantee the outcomes of such battles except by fiat, so the ST may need some other event that interferes.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3046,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","user":"Black Fox","date":". 09-02-2023, 04:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}